  "version": "0.6.1-beta.2",
  "notes": "## Changes since `v0.6.1-beta.1`\n\n### Fixes\n\n- recognize an SFTP drag out dropped on a File Explorer folder whose path is longer than 260 characters, since the shell's create notice was read into a MAX_PATH buffer with SHGetPathFromIDListW and failed for deep folders, so the drop was reported as landing on an unknown target; SHGetPathFromIDListEx now reads it into a buffer sized for the longest path Windows allows ([ede17675](https://github.com/330079598/tTerm/commit/ede176759023f3f33af251815a7177d896bfa677))\n- have File Explorer show what an SFTP drag out downloaded without a manual refresh, since right after its own copy of the drop placeholders it could miss the file system's notices for the placeholder delete and the download's part file, rename and sidecar delete, leaving stale entries until F5: each deleted placeholder is now announced to the shell with SHCNE_DELETE or SHCNE_RMDIR, and once the download into the dropped-on folder ends, even if it failed, the new refresh_drop_folder command sends SHCNE_UPDATEDIR so the folder is listed again; macOS leaves Finder to follow the folder itself ([bac289a8](https://github.com/330079598/tTerm/commit/bac289a848c40ba248b92d34df650afca1b48c05))\n\n**Full comparison:** [v0.6.1-beta.1...v0.6.1-beta.2](https://github.com/330079598/tTerm/compare/v0.6.1-beta.1...v0.6.1-beta.2)",
